  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is added and works as `@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())`. The full suite passes (1912 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n- **Parsing:** it splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')` and `a=` gives `('a', '')`. An empty value is allowed.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or with an empty key fails with `'nokey' is not a valid key=value pair.`, and the empty string `''` fails the same way.\n- **`multiple=True`:** it works with this option setting and returns a tuple of pairs.\n\nThe class is in `src/click/types.py` and exported from `src/click/__init__.py`. I added tests for valid and invalid input to `tests/test_types.py`.",
